Maya: Heads-up  planning to split the big structured-output doc into: (A) JSON schemas + portable examples, (B) parsing patterns + SDK snippets + fallback heuristics. Smaller diffs should speed reviews.

Jon: Good call. I'll own A (schemas/examples). I'll add a compact AJV example and a short note about nullable arrays.

Kat: I'll take B (parsing + SDK). Plan: concise tryParse envelope snippet for SDK v4, a tiny regex fallback example, and a short paragraph on when function-calling is preferable.

Rafael: I'll run a link sweep and prepare a redirects-only PR for moved example paths. If schema PR lands first we should merge redirects right after.

LintBot: CI note: please add language tags to fenced code blocks and remove trailing commas in JSON examples; these will fail the docs linter.

Maya: Timeline: drafts tomorrow, aim to land both by Friday. Keep snippets minimal and copy-paste safe.

Jon: PR A opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1200. Moved examples to docs/schemas/ and added frontmatter. Left TODO for small lint fixes.

Kat: PR B draft: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1201. Includes SDK v4 parse fallback snippet:```js
// SDK v4 minimal parse fallback
try {
  return JSON.parse(text);
} catch (e) {
  const m = /\"result\"\s*:\s*\"([^\"]+)\"/.exec(text);
  return m ? {result: m[1]} : {raw: text, parseError: true};
}
```

Kat: Added a short warning: fallback regex is best-effort, avoid for regulated/PII data.

Rafael: Redirects PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1202 (sidebar updates + redirect map).

Jon: fixed lint nits and merged PR A.

Kat: addressed wording and merged PR B after a quick review. Added SDK 3.x -> 4.x one-liner migration note in PR description.

Rafael: merged redirects PR and updated the release-notes draft.

Maya: Please add a one-line release note: "Docs: split structured-output into schema and parsing guides; added SDK v4 parsing fallback examples and redirects."

Jon: Added the blurb. Closing thread. :tada:
